{"name":"Chamomile","hex":"#e4c697","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"chamomile","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["US standard spelling of camomile."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/chamomile"}],"entries":[{"title":"Chamomile","blocks":[{"text":"Chamomile or camomile is the common name for several daisy-like plants of the family Asteraceae. Two of the species, Matricaria chamomilla and Chamaemelum nobile, are commonly used to make herbal infusions for beverages. Chamomile is used as a flavoring in foods, beverages, and cosmetics, in herbal teas, in brewing beer, and as a ground cover or seating plant in gardens."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/26/Kamomillasaunio_%28Matricaria_recutita%29.JPG/330px-Kamomillasaunio_%28Matricaria_recutita%29.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Chamomile","wikidata":"Q14169150"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/6e/Chamaemelum_nobile_001.JPG/500px-Chamaemelum_nobile_001.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/6e/Chamaemelum_nobile_001.JPG/1280px-Chamaemelum_nobile_001.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/6e/Chamaemelum_nobile_001.JPG/500px-Chamaemelum_nobile_001.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Roman chamomile, Chamaemelum nobile","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AChamaemelum_nobile_001.JPG"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d4/Loose_leaf_chamomile_tea.jpg/500px-Loose_leaf_chamomile_tea.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d4/Loose_leaf_chamomile_tea.jpg/1280px-Loo